        "uuid": "4ba1bf8b_9bafed71",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/hlsl/writer/raise/promote_initializers_fuzz.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-26T16:27:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doesn\u0027t this need `kPromoteInitializerCapabilites` as well in the `post capabilities? I guess the question is, should the `post` be a superset of the `pre`?",
      "revId": "af687e0b966c43130e8abe1f35dcd216a9e22d63",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "151406ab_4905227d",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/hlsl/writer/raise/promote_initializers_fuzz.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-26T17:38:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As a general rule, I think post needs to be a superset of pre, since otherwise if the transform is a no-op, there would be the possibility that an IR state that passes validation before would fail after without any modification.\n\nThe one exception that I can think of for this is a transform that is explicitly designed to remove specific constructs, which might narrow the capabilities, if it meant to guarantee all of a specific pattern/construct is not present after it runs. (In this case a no-op would indicate that the capability wasn\u0027t actually used in the input).\n\nAre there any transforms like this, that intentionally narrow capabilities?\n\n(if not/we don\u0027t expect there to be any, I could add an assert to ::Create that guarantees that post_capabilities is a superset of pre_capabilities to catch programming errors like this)",
      "parentUuid": "4ba1bf8b_9bafed71",
      "revId": "af687e0b966c43130e8abe1f35dcd216a9e22d63",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25d893e9_b67ad5e5",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/hlsl/writer/raise/promote_initializers_fuzz.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-26T18:02:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking about it, I think there are basically 2 cases.\n\n1- the lowering passes, pre is a superset, as we\u0027re lowering down to core and removing frontend specific constructs\n2- the raise passes, post is a superset, as we\u0027re rasing up to core and adding backend specific constructs\n\nSo, i don\u0027t know if a general assert would work. \n\n@jrprice@google.com did i miss any cases here?",
      "parentUuid": "151406ab_4905227d",
      "revId": "af687e0b966c43130e8abe1f35dcd216a9e22d63",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b536a0d_cd2c8aee",
        "filename": "src/tint/lang/hlsl/writer/raise/promote_initializers_fuzz.cc",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002241
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-26T19:30:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even for Raise, I don\u0027t think we can/should guarantee that the post capabilities are a superset of the pre capabilities, since a backend-specific transform may be removing the use of something that is valid in core (e.g. RemoveTerminatorArgs - although we don\u0027t have a capability for terminator args right now we certainly could add one).",
      "parentUuid": "25d893e9_b67ad5e5",
      "revId": "af687e0b966c43130e8abe1f35dcd216a9e22d63",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
